# Build context exclusions. The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so ANYTHING not
# listed here ends up in the image — keep local-only, regenerable and private
# material out. When you add a local-only directory to .gitignore, add it here
# too; the two lists overlap but are not the same (this one also drops the .git
# directory itself and the host-side launchers).
#
# NB: a line here is a pattern, not a pattern plus a comment — `#` only starts a
# comment at the beginning of a line.

# --- never bake a database into the image ------------------------------------
# The container creates its own at /app/data/db.sqlite3 on first boot.
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-wal
db.sqlite3-shm
**/db.sqlite3
**/db.sqlite3-wal
**/db.sqlite3-shm
data/

# --- virtualenvs and byte-code caches (host-built, wrong platform, huge) -----
.venv/
.venv-linux/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo

# --- version control ----------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- agent scaffolding and regenerable outputs --------------------------------
_ai/
previews/
.preview_state.json
.preview_config.json

# --- private / host-specific / never needed at run time -----------------------
MACMINI_HOSTING.md
.env
*.command
*.log
*.bak
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
